---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '1 November 2026';
const toc = [
  { id: 'general', label: 'General information only' },
  { id: 'no-advice', label: 'No professional or engineering advice' },
  { id: 'accuracy', label: 'Accuracy, completeness and currency' },
  { id: 'oe-references', label: 'OE references and trademarks' },
  { id: 'images', label: 'Images and illustrations' },
  { id: 'external-links', label: 'External links' },
  { id: 'no-warranty', label: 'No warranty and limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'verify', label: 'Verify before you order' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="How to read China Filter Hub data: the limits of compiled specifications and OE cross-references, trademarks, and checks before ordering."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer/' }]}
  updated="2026-11-01"
>
  <LegalPage
    title="Disclaimer"
    updated={updated}
    toc={toc}
    intro="This page explains the status of the information published on China Filter Hub, the limits of cross-reference data, and the checks a buyer should complete before placing an order. It applies to every product, specification and reference page on the site."
  >
    <h2 id="general">1. General information only</h2>
    <p>
      The content of this website is provided for general information and sourcing purposes. It is
      not a contractual specification, a certificate of conformity, or a statement that a product is
      suitable for a particular vehicle, machine or process. Binding specifications exist only in
      the documents issued with a confirmed order.
    </p>

    <h2 id="no-advice">2. No professional or engineering advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site constitutes engineering, safety, legal, customs or regulatory advice.
      Filtration requirements depend on the medium being filtered, the operating conditions, the
      equipment manufacturer&rsquo;s requirements and the rules of the destination market — factors
      we cannot assess from a web page. Where a decision carries safety, warranty or regulatory
      consequences, confirm it with a qualified engineer or with the equipment manufacturer.
    </p>

    <h2 id="accuracy">3. Accuracy, completeness and currency</h2>
    <p>
      Specifications are compiled from manufacturer catalogues, published standards and supplier
      documentation. Each field is recorded with a data-status label describing how the value was
      obtained; where a value could not be traced to a source, the field is left blank rather than
      estimated or inferred.
    </p>
    <p>
      Compilation has inherent limits. Catalogues contain errors. Part numbers are revised,
      superseded or reused across model years. A filter that fits one variant of an engine may not
      fit another built in a different plant or year. Information on this site may therefore be
      incomplete, out of date, or in specific cases incorrect, and it is published without any
      representation that it is free of error.
    </p>

    <h2 id="oe-references">4. OE references and trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      OE numbers, competitor part numbers and manufacturer names are reproduced for identification
      only. A recorded cross-reference means that a part has been associated with that number in a
      catalogue or supplier document. It does <strong>not</strong> establish dimensional equivalence,
      material equivalence, filtration performance equivalence, or the existence of any approval by
      the original manufacturer.
    </p>
    <p>
      All trademarks, brand names and part numbers remain the property of their respective owners.
      They are used descriptively, to identify the application a part is intended for, and their use
      does not imply affiliation with, endorsement by, or approval of this site or its operator by
      any manufacturer. If you are a rights holder and believe a reference on this site is
      mislabelled, contact us and we will review it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="images">5. Images and illustrations</h2>
    <p>
      Some product and facility images on this site are computer-generated illustrations created for
      presentation. They do not depict an actual production facility, an actual shipment, or the
      exact appearance of the product you would receive. Where a photograph of a real product is
      shown, the accompanying specification — not the image — governs the description.
    </p>

    <h2 id="external-links">6. External links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to external websites are provided for convenience and reference. We do not control those
      sites and accept no responsibility for their content, accuracy, availability or practices.
      Following an external link is at your own discretion.
    </p>

    <h2 id="no-warranty">7. No warranty and limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      The site and its content are provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; basis, without warranties of
      any kind, express or implied, to the extent permitted by law. We are not liable for loss
      arising from reliance on information published here, including a part ordered on the basis of
      an unverified cross-reference.
    </p>
    <p>
      This does not affect the warranties that apply to goods supplied under a contract of sale,
      which are set out in that contract, nor any liability that cannot lawfully be excluded. The
      full liability provisions are in our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="verify">8. Verify before you order</h2>
    <p>
      Before committing to an order, confirm the following against a source you trust:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dimensions</strong> — outer and inner diameter, height, thread or connection type, and gasket profile, checked against the OE drawing or a physical sample.</li>
      <li><strong>Application</strong> — engine code, model year, plant of manufacture and any market-specific variant, not only the vehicle model name.</li>
      <li><strong>Media and efficiency</strong> — the filtration rating and media type required by the equipment manufacturer, particularly where warranty or safety applies.</li>
      <li><strong>Standards and marking</strong> — any standard the destination market requires, and whether the product is marked accordingly.</li>
      <li><strong>Packaging and labelling</strong> — for private-label or OEM supply, the agreed artwork, language and traceability marking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If a value on this site is marked as unverified or is missing, ask us before assuming it. We
      would rather send a drawing than have you order against a number that has not been confirmed.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">9. Changes to this disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this page as the site&rsquo;s data model or the applicable rules change. The
      date at the top of the page shows the current version.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      To query a specification, report an error, or raise a trademark concern:
    </p>
    <p>
      {site.entity.legalName}<br />
      {site.entity.address}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.entity.email}`}>{site.entity.email}</a> ·{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.entity.emailAlt}`}>{site.entity.emailAlt}</a><br />
      Telephone / WhatsApp: {site.entity.phone}
    </p>
    <p class="muted small">
      See also: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> · <a href="/company/">Company details</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
